// CoRR+sync -- read-read coherence over writes of two threads. The second
// write is made after reading the flag the first write is published with, so
// it happens after the first and follows it in co (CoWW). A third thread then
// reads 2 and then 1. OCaml allows it: non-atomic reads need not be coherent.
// RC11 forbids it: po between the reads, then fr and rf, is a cycle in hb;eco.
// Unlike CoRR.lit, the writes are in two threads.
//
// The OCaml memory model (Dolan, Sivaramakrishnan & Madhavapeddy, PLDI 2018,
// section 6). An access in mode sc is to an atomic location, any other access
// non-atomic.
a := 0;
f := 0;
{
  a := 1;
  f.store(1, sc)
} ||| {
  rf := f.load(sc);
  if (rf = 1) {
    a := 2
  }
} ||| {
  r1 := a;
  r2 := a
}
%%
allow (rf = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [OCaml]
forbid (rf = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [RC11]
forbid (rf = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [smrd]
